                <pb facs="0494" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Public Works Debt/141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-19T19:00:00-05:00">October 19, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Your No. 117, October 19, 1 p.m. In view of the discussions now in progress
                    here between the Cuban Ambassador and the Under Secretary, I do not believe that
                    any further exposition of the position of this Government by the Embassy is
                    necessary or would be desirable at this juncture. You should accordingly avoid
                    for the moment further conversations, on the subject of the specific questions
                    under discussion here, with officials of the Cuban Government, and should such
                    conversations be proposed by the latter I prefer that you courteously suggest
                    that they do not appear to be required in the light of the Washington
                    discussions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
